$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=isumcollcvg  LOC_AFTER=?

* Convergence of a series is unchanged by collapsing the zero terms off the range of a strictly increasing map (isercoll at the level of dom ~~>).

h1::isumcollcvg.g |- ( ph -> G : NN --> NN )
h2::isumcollcvg.i |- ( ( ph /\ k e. NN ) -> ( G ` k ) < ( G ` ( k + 1 ) ) )
h3::isumcollcvg.0 |- ( ( ph /\ n e. ( NN \ ran G ) ) -> ( F ` n ) = 0 )
h4::isumcollcvg.f |- ( ( ph /\ n e. NN ) -> ( F ` n ) e. CC )
h5::isumcollcvg.h |- ( ( ph /\ k e. NN ) -> ( H ` k ) = ( F ` ( G ` k ) ) )
